id: E6407
draft: true
title: "Strict patch-ng context bytes must match the pristine source"
category: conan, patch_ng, unified-diff, ohos, source
match_keywords: >
  hunk no.1 doesn't match, source file is different, Failed to apply patch,
  patch_ng strict context, git apply whitespace tolerance, cumulative preimage
root_cause: >
  Conan's apply_conandata_patches uses patch_ng with strip=0 and fuzz=False.
  The matcher compares context bytes at the declared hunk offset, while git
  apply may tolerate a leading-whitespace difference. A patch can therefore
  pass a local git replay but fail in the production source phase.
error_signature: >
  hunk no.1 doesn't match, source file is different, ConanException: Failed to
  apply patch, expected context differs from actual indentation
trigger_tool: conan, patch_ng, git
phase: source
severity: 2
rec_approach: >
  Recreate a fresh pristine source tree, apply the complete conandata order
  through patch_ng 1.19.1 with strip=0 and fuzz=False, inspect every context
  record byte-for-byte at its hunk offset, correct only the mismatching bytes,
  and rerun the complete ordered replay. Keep failed and corrected trees
  immutable and separate.
rec_description: >
  This pattern covers any Conan recipe whose source phase applies unified diffs
  with a strict Python patcher. It is not limited to dosbox or to indentation:
  blank-line markers, line endings, and cumulative hunk offsets require the
  same exact-preimage validation. A git or GNU patch dry-run alone is not a
  production compatibility proof.
verification_cmd: >
  patch_ng.fromfile(patch).apply(strip=0, root=pristine_copy, fuzz=False) for
  every ordered patch, followed by a fresh conan create and postimage hash
  comparison.
affected_scope: >
  Conan 2.x recipes using apply_conandata_patches or another strict unified-diff
  parser against release archives and cumulative patch chains.
safety_boundary: >
  Never enable fuzzing to hide a mismatch, reuse a partially patched recipe
  cache, modify an immutable failed evidence tree, or report CI success before
  a current-commit conan create completes.
doc_file: knowledge/drafts/E6407-draft-2301_80739235.md
last_updated: 2026-09-13
authors: 2301_80739235
